$CATEGORY: Vocabulary/HansenQuinn/2.4

::Q001::[markdown]ἆρα:{
	~%100%introduces a question#Correct: **ἆρα** → “introduces a question” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%away from#Incorrect. **ἀπό + gen** means “away from” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%here#Incorrect. **ἐνταῦθα** means “here” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%whenever#Incorrect. **ἐπειδάν** means “whenever” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%(with participle, the speaker believes this)#Incorrect. **ἅτε** means “(with participle, the speaker believes this)” (Chapter 8).
}


::Q002::[markdown]either… or:{
	~%100%ἤ… ἤ#Correct: **ἤ… ἤ** → “either… or” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%μή#Incorrect. **μή** means “not” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%καίπερ#Incorrect. **καίπερ** means “although” (Chapter 8).
	~%-100%ἐπειδή#Incorrect. **ἐπειδή** means “after” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%οὖν#Incorrect. **οὖν** means “therefore” (Chapter 7).
}


::Q003::[markdown]host:{
	~%-100%καιρός, καιροῦ, ὁ#Incorrect. **καιρός, καιροῦ, ὁ** means “right moment” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%κάλλος, κάλλους, τό#Incorrect. **κάλλος, κάλλους, τό** means “beauty” (Chapter 11).
	~%100%ξένος, ξένου, ὁ#Correct: **ξένος, ξένου, ὁ** → “host” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%δῶρον, δώρου, τό#Incorrect. **δῶρον, δώρου, τό** means “gift” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%βίος, βίου, ὁ#Incorrect. **βίος, βίου, ὁ** means “life” (Chapter 9).
}


::Q004::[markdown]λύσω:{
	~%50%free#Correct: **λύσω** is Principal Part 2 of **λύω** “free” (Chapter 2).
	~%50%unbind#Correct: **λύσω** is Principal Part 2 of **λύω** “unbind” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%win#Incorrect. **νικάω** is Principal Part 1 of **νικάω** “win” (Chapter 9).
	~%-100%welcome#Incorrect. **δέχομαι** is Principal Part 1 of **δέχομαι** “welcome” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%show#Incorrect. **δηλόω** is Principal Part 1 of **δηλόω** “show” (Chapter 10).
}


::Q005::[markdown]now:{
	~%-100%εἴθε; εἰ γάρ#Incorrect. **εἴθε; εἰ γάρ** means “introduces optative of wish” (Chapter 7).
	~%-100%γε#Incorrect. **γε** means “at any rate” (Chapter 6).
	~%-100%ὅμως#Incorrect. **ὅμως** means “nevertheless” (Chapter 8).
	~%-100%ἆρα#Incorrect. **ἆρα** means “introduces a question” (Chapter 2).
	~%100%νῦν#Correct: **νῦν** → “now” (Chapter 2).
}


